spec:
  grid: 27-30 rows x 30 cols, background 0
  components: 1 multicolor exemplar + 1-2 solid target rectangles, all non-overlapping, separated by >=1 bg
  exemplar:
    size: 9-11 rows x 11-16 cols
    colors: 3-4 distinct (including outer color)
    corners: all four corners share the same outer_color
    structure: banded pattern of identical-row runs (axis 0) and identical-col runs (axis 1)
    row_runs: 1-5 distinct bands, col_runs: 3-7 distinct bands
    each run is a group of consecutive identical rows (or cols); run widths 1-5
    stretch_run: per axis, exactly one run has strictly more unique colors than all others (or if tied, is uniquely the widest); this is the stretchable interior band
    symmetry: LR and/or UD [observed] (3/4 examples show at least one axis of symmetry)
  targets:
    each is a solid rectangle filled with exemplar.outer_color
    size: 7-15 rows x 9-16 cols
    constraint: target_h > fixed_rows AND target_w > fixed_cols (so stretch band has positive width in both axes)
  output:
    same grid size; each target rectangle replaced by the exemplar pattern stretched to target dimensions
    stretching: per axis, all runs keep their original width except the stretch run, which absorbs the size difference

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size ~27-30 x 30, bg=0. Choose 3-4 non-bg colors; designate one as outer_color.
    2. Build exemplar pattern as banded rectangles. For each axis, create 1-7 runs of identical lines with widths 1-5. Ensure exactly one run per axis has strictly more unique colors in its line than all other runs (or is uniquely widest if tied). All four corners must be outer_color.
    3. Compute fixed_rows/fixed_cols (sum of non-stretch run widths per axis).
    4. Generate 1-2 target rectangles with dimensions > (fixed_rows, fixed_cols). Each target is solid outer_color.
    5. Place exemplar and targets on the grid with >=1 bg gap between all pairs and to grid edges. No overlapping.
    6. Input = grid with solid outer_color targets. Output = grid with targets replaced by stretched exemplar.
